WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:04.270
-Here he is, Blake Shelton.
Oh, my gosh, this is fantastic.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.806
-Whoo! Jimmy!
-Nice to see you.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.808
Nice to see you, buddy.

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:09.809
Where are you?

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.678
You got a lot of animals
back there.

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:16.282
-I'm in Oklahoma
at my place here.

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:18.451
And what did you say,
I got a lot of animals?

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.485
I do have a dog --

00:00:19.485 --> 00:00:20.686
-Yeah, I saw --
-Betty, come here.

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:21.854
Come here.
-I saw a dog, aw.

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:24.624
-I got Betty here.
-That's a beautiful dog.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.592
Oh, my -- oh, what a good dog.

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:30.396
-Oh, my God, your breath
smells like Jimmy.

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:33.700
-Oh, my gosh.
Who are you there with?

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.435
Who are you being safe with?

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:41.340
-We are quarantined
with a bunch of Stefanis.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.277
I'm talking about
a pile of them.

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:48.247
It's me and a bunch of Stefanis.

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:52.452
My mom and stepdad live,

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:53.986
I don't know,
about 10 miles from here.

00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:58.324
I haven't seen them
since the middle of March,

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.092
except for waving at them,
you know,

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:03.029
through the truck window.

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:04.297
And that's about it.

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:05.865
We haven't left.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.666
-Yeah, it's kind of --
it's weird.

00:01:07.666 --> 00:01:10.370
-I had to cancel my tour.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:13.005
We were in Omaha, Nebraska.

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:16.742
And we were actually building
the production that day.

00:01:16.742 --> 00:01:19.779
And finally just decided, that's
when pretty much the bottom

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:24.050
was falling out of all touring
and any live events.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.219
And so we just cancelled,
and Gwen and I

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:28.253
immediately came here
and we have not left.

00:01:28.253 --> 00:01:30.923
-What have you been doing

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:32.858
with all --
with your downtime?

00:01:32.858 --> 00:01:35.027
It feels like the days go fast,
really, huh?

00:01:35.027 --> 00:01:37.363
-Oh, my God, they do.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.731
They go by so fast.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:43.269
And a lot of us, because I black
out normally around

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:46.439
5:30 or 6:00 or something --

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:50.310
yeah, you like my hat,
by the way?

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:54.747
-Get closer, I can't see it.
-"I drank today."

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.717
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:58.852
Hey, that's not bad.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.286
-That's pretty much all we do,
you know?

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.989
Gwen has learned
how to bake bread

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.657
really good, sourdough bread.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:08.995
We're just -- literally it's
like, you know,

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:10.696
"Little House on the Prairie"
out here.

00:02:10.696 --> 00:02:14.033
Like, she makes bread.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:18.370
I've been building a fence
and gardening.

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:21.908
And we're pretty self-sufficient
out here.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:24.910
As a matter of fact,
I don't know --

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.578
this interview,
I wanted to do it,

00:02:26.578 --> 00:02:29.749
but we actually have a schedule

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:32.551
that we already
had lined out for today.

00:02:32.551 --> 00:02:34.453
And I don't think
we can put it off any longer.

00:02:34.453 --> 00:02:36.289
It's up to you, if you just want
to go ahead and start.

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:41.127
-Hey, Jimmy.
-Oh, my -- yay! Finally!

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.795
-We talked a lot about this.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:46.232
Yeah, I'm going to be helping
Blake grow out his mullet.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:49.669
So, you know, today we already
scheduled it was haircut day.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:52.905
So, I have my clippers.

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:57.276
I got my attachments.
-Oh, my God.

00:02:57.276 --> 00:02:58.144
-I got to get a haircut.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.545
But go ahead with your questions

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:02.147
'cause you're a very good,
interesting interviewer.

00:03:02.147 --> 00:03:04.850
And I don't want to miss...
-Oh, my God.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.887
-...any of the good things
that you got to ask me.

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.855
-Thank gosh you took off
that camouflaged jacket

00:03:09.855 --> 00:03:11.357
'cause I didn't --
I noticed

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:13.226
I didn't think
you had arms for a second.

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:15.695
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.229
-Oh, my God.

00:03:17.229 --> 00:03:19.598
Are you gonna give him a mullet?
Please give him a mullet.

00:03:19.598 --> 00:03:21.567
Please.
-Yeah.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:22.902
-Blake, this is
really interesting --

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.704
I love seeing
Gwen cut your hair.

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:26.072
This is fantastic.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.406
I love this.

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:29.975
Hey, are you guys, like --
do you guys give,

00:03:29.975 --> 00:03:32.145
like,
give each other inspiration

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:33.546
on new music,
like, different music?

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.914
'Cause I know you have different
backgrounds musically.

00:03:35.914 --> 00:03:37.016
Like, what have you --

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.551
what music are you
listening to, Gwen,

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:42.521
that you wouldn't have listened
to before Blake and vice versa?

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:44.323
-The music that Blake
turned me on to,

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:46.259
it's called country music.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:49.895
Yeah, I hadn't really
listened to much of that

00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:51.930
on my ska playlist.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:55.835
But it's been fun learning
about country music,

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:57.236
and all the different --

00:03:57.236 --> 00:04:01.907
He's literally an encyclopedia
jukebox, like a weirdo.

00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:03.776
Like a weirdo
with the knowledge.

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:07.146
-Every country?
-This guy, he knows everything.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:08.714
Like -- and we do games with him
where we'll

00:04:08.714 --> 00:04:10.115
just, like,
play, like,

00:04:10.115 --> 00:04:12.518
a little tiny taste of a song
to see if he will know it.

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:13.886
And we won't know what it is.

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:16.122
We'll just look it up on, like,
the Internet.

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:17.357
And he'll know it.

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:18.958
-The only time I've ever been
stumped on that,

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:21.894
is on your show, whenever
y'all played something --

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:26.098
like the "Welcome Back, Kotter"
version of "Hollaback Girl"

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:27.499
or whatever it was.

00:04:27.499 --> 00:04:29.434
I didn't know --
-"Welcome back, Kotter" version?

00:04:29.434 --> 00:04:31.604
You didn't even know your
girlfriend's song at the time.

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:34.340
-No, it was -- y'all played
some weird version of it

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.574
I never heard of before.

00:04:35.574 --> 00:04:37.610
-I forgave him, though.
-Yeah.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.912
-Blake, who --
what is the Conway Twitty song

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:42.315
where he sounds like Elvis?

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:45.718
-Oh, that's --
♪ People see us everywhere ♪

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:47.119
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:47.119 --> 00:04:49.855
♪ -They think you really ♪
"It's Only Make Believe."

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:52.358
That's it.
-I love that song.

00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:58.865
-It was a pop rock song.

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:01.200
That's what he had
his first success with.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.603
And then later, he went country.

00:05:04.603 --> 00:05:06.639
-I would love it if Gwen would
not come back

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.641
and just left you with
that haircut.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.142
-What did he say?

00:05:10.142 --> 00:05:13.746
-I said Conway started out rock
and pop and then went country

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:17.316
kind of like Gwen Stefani.
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:18.884
-Gwen has a country
hit right now.

00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:20.386
We have a duet.
-Whoo!

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:23.789
-Who would have ever thought
Gwen Stefani on country radio?

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:25.157
-I know.
I love it.

00:05:25.157 --> 00:05:26.826
I think it's so --
Do you love singing it, Gwen?

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:28.894
It comes -- It feels natural.

00:05:28.894 --> 00:05:30.996
-It was one of those songs
that I was like,

00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:33.498
"Wow, you just" --
these songs come to Blake.

00:05:33.498 --> 00:05:35.300
They're so incredible.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.903
And I was dreaming
that I could be on it.

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:39.338
We were working out together
in the gym.

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:41.774
And I was like, "Man, I wish
you'd put me on this one."

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:44.109
He actually turned
the song off and goes,

00:05:44.109 --> 00:05:45.444
"Dang, I wish
I would put you on this one."

00:05:45.444 --> 00:05:47.346
And then he did.
So here we are.

00:05:47.346 --> 00:05:50.116
-Was it written as a duet
when it first --

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:54.219
-It wasn't. It was just --
No, it wasn't, was it?

00:05:54.219 --> 00:05:57.690
-No, but what's crazy is that
one of the writers,

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:01.126
Shane, had sent me the song
to give to Blake.

00:06:01.126 --> 00:06:02.861
Like, one of those,
he had my text

00:06:02.861 --> 00:06:05.965
and he wanted me
to give it to him.

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:10.303
So it was a weird coincidence,
the whole thing.

00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:13.205
-Are you getting him
into ska music at all?

00:06:13.205 --> 00:06:16.475
-I tried.
I made him a ska playlist.

00:06:16.475 --> 00:06:20.646
We were listening to a bunch
of reggae and UB-40.

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:24.517
We were building actually
a garden out here the other day.

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:28.320
We had, like, everybody on it,
pulling rocks and planting.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.823
And we were listening to a lot
of that music that day.

00:06:30.823 --> 00:06:32.791
So, did you like it?
-Yes.

00:06:32.791 --> 00:06:34.993
-You got to get him to --

00:06:34.993 --> 00:06:36.429
-We had Steel Pulse playing,
Jimmy.

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:38.897
That's a band you probably
never heard of.

00:06:38.897 --> 00:06:42.568
But they're very popular
in the ska world.

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:47.506
-I know Steel Pulse.

00:06:47.506 --> 00:06:50.610
My jam is "Ghost Town."

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:53.212
Is that Specials?
-Yeah.

00:06:53.212 --> 00:06:54.880
-Blake, you'd like that one,
I think.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.582
-Yeah, I do.
That's the one that goes...

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:59.785
[ Vocalizes ]

00:06:59.785 --> 00:07:01.420
You're right.
I do love that song.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:05.457
-Oh, my God, Gwen, I don't know
how you put up with this dude.

00:07:05.457 --> 00:07:07.760
-Just learning, Jimmy,
but I already know that much.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.795
-Can you come closer
to the camera

00:07:09.795 --> 00:07:12.397
so I can see your haircut?

00:07:12.397 --> 00:07:16.068
-Closer up.
-Yeah.

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:19.104
-Like shamish.

00:07:19.104 --> 00:07:21.574
-How's the mullet? Is the mullet
getting long in the back?

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:23.876
-Not long enough, man.
You can get it longer.

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:25.511
But it's getting close.

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:26.912
I like those sides coming off.

00:07:26.912 --> 00:07:28.514
This looks really good.

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:29.748
I've never seen you like this.

00:07:29.748 --> 00:07:32.317
-You know, to be able to do this
to the greatest,

00:07:32.317 --> 00:07:34.319
all-time greatest country star.

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:41.693
-Whoo!
♪ People see us everywhere ♪

00:07:41.693 --> 00:07:45.430
-We're highlighting
a different charity

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:47.299
from everyone that's
on our show tonight.

00:07:47.299 --> 00:07:50.636
-Yeah.
-And you chose MusiCares.

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:52.171
-Yeah.

00:07:52.171 --> 00:07:57.709 line:0%
-So if you go to
grammy.com/musicares --

00:07:57.709 --> 00:08:00.579 line:0%
It's a long --
it's a lot of words.

00:08:00.579 --> 00:08:01.746 line:0%
I'll just put it up
on the screen.

00:08:01.746 --> 00:08:03.649 line:0%
-Put it up on the screen.

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:05.818 line:0%
-Hey, really quickly,
can we talk about

00:08:05.818 --> 00:08:08.053
"The Voice" while
you're getting your haircut?

00:08:08.053 --> 00:08:09.955
-Let's do it.
No, what's scary is

00:08:09.955 --> 00:08:12.191
we're going to have to do
"The Voice"

00:08:12.191 --> 00:08:15.861
in some fashion like this,
because obviously, you know,

00:08:15.861 --> 00:08:20.065
the live shows are coming up
here in just a matter of weeks.

00:08:20.065 --> 00:08:22.401
And especially in L.A.,

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:25.137
we're not going to be
ready to, you know,

00:08:25.137 --> 00:08:26.805
to have events again.

00:08:26.805 --> 00:08:28.707
So it's going to be crazy.

00:08:28.707 --> 00:08:30.208
We're going to have to coach
like this.

00:08:30.208 --> 00:08:32.577
It's just going to have
to work out this way.

00:08:32.577 --> 00:08:33.779
It's going to be nuts.

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.113
-Have you talked about it?

00:08:35.113 --> 00:08:39.585
Have you -- do you have a plan?
-Yeah, a little bit.

00:08:39.585 --> 00:08:41.386
I think they do.

00:08:41.386 --> 00:08:42.788
I just kind of like --

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:45.057
Gwen's brother actually set up
this computer

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:47.226
and this interview
and everything for me today

00:08:47.226 --> 00:08:50.596
because I clearly don't know
how to do this stuff.

00:08:50.596 --> 00:08:54.567
So I think they have a plan,
and they're going to tell me

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:56.268
when to be at the computer.

00:08:56.268 --> 00:08:57.703
And I -- you know,
I'll listen to them

00:08:57.703 --> 00:09:00.739
I guess perform, and then
give them some pointers.

00:09:00.739 --> 00:09:02.541
And I don't know.

00:09:02.541 --> 00:09:04.243
This is a --

00:09:04.243 --> 00:09:07.313
we're having to do things
that -- how does it look?

00:09:07.313 --> 00:09:08.381
-I think it looks good.

00:09:08.381 --> 00:09:09.515
-You look like
you're really handling

00:09:09.515 --> 00:09:12.685
this whole quarantine well.

00:09:12.685 --> 00:09:14.686
-Is that a joke about my weight?

00:09:14.686 --> 00:09:16.856
That's a fat joke, isn't it,
Jimmy?

00:09:16.856 --> 00:09:18.524
That's a fat joke, isn't it?

00:09:18.524 --> 00:09:20.725
-No, it's not --
-You're right, though.

00:09:20.725 --> 00:09:21.860
-It's not that at all.

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:24.896
It's just --
-Is that a good angle?

00:09:24.896 --> 00:09:26.565
-Oh, my God.
No, no, no.

00:09:26.565 --> 00:09:28.767
I'm -- Dude, you gone punk.

00:09:28.767 --> 00:09:30.369
Your hair's punk.

00:09:30.369 --> 00:09:32.471
Crazy, man.
That's what happens to a man.

00:09:32.471 --> 00:09:33.739
-Love it.

00:09:33.739 --> 00:09:35.641
-We get to see the real
Blake Shelton, finally.

00:09:35.641 --> 00:09:38.177
-Hey, will you --
one last request,

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:40.512
will you put a J

00:09:40.512 --> 00:09:43.148
and an F here
for Jimmy Fallon?

00:09:43.148 --> 00:09:44.450
Please?

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:47.586
Please, please.
-Sure.

00:09:47.586 --> 00:09:49.388
-I'm so happy to see
both of you guys,

00:09:49.388 --> 00:09:52.091
and I got to tell everyone
watching at home,

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:55.861
"Nobody But You" is the song
from the album

00:09:55.861 --> 00:09:59.331
"Fully Loaded: God's Country,"
but it is so beautiful,

00:09:59.331 --> 00:10:02.768
and you guys do it so well,
and I actually --

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:04.769
I showed it
to my wife earlier today.

00:10:04.769 --> 00:10:07.272
'Cause you guys just recorded
it for us, thank you.

00:10:07.272 --> 00:10:09.775
But I loved it.
Great performance.

00:10:09.775 --> 00:10:12.744
-We did, just for you.
-I know, my name --

00:10:12.744 --> 00:10:15.448
I think you mentioned my name,
"Hey, Jimmy," I think you said.

00:10:15.448 --> 00:10:16.816
-I'm literally putting
your initials

00:10:16.816 --> 00:10:18.050
in my head right now, Jimmy.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:19.184
I'm not kidding.

00:10:19.184 --> 00:10:21.486
-See, these are why
these shows are fun

00:10:21.486 --> 00:10:24.456
because you would never
do this in real life.

00:10:24.456 --> 00:10:26.291
-She just said they're not
showing up very well

00:10:26.291 --> 00:10:27.760
because of the gray.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:30.129
-[ Laughs ]

00:10:30.129 --> 00:10:33.932
-Oh, no, that looks terrible.
-Blake, get right in there.

00:10:33.932 --> 00:10:36.935
Get real close
so I can really see it.

00:10:36.935 --> 00:10:38.770
Yeah.
-There's the F,

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:41.807
and here's the J.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:10:41.807 --> 00:10:45.578
Dude, you are so "Tiger King"
right now, you have no idea.

00:10:45.578 --> 00:10:47.012
[ Laughter ]

00:10:47.012 --> 00:10:50.949
I love you guys,

00:10:50.949 --> 00:10:53.319
and stay safe, okay?
-We love you.

00:10:53.319 --> 00:10:56.088
Thanks for having us
on "The Tonight Show" today.

00:10:56.088 --> 00:10:57.656
-I love you guys.
"The Tonight Show" today.

00:10:57.656 --> 00:10:59.291
Come back, can't wait to see you
in person again.

